#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:12
msgid "Code Scrub Methodology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:14
msgid "Core principle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:16
msgid ""
"Scrubbing improves code quality by **removing waste** — not by adding "
"abstractions. Every change must make the code simpler, not more complex. "
"If a fix introduces more indirection than it removes duplication, don't "
"make it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:18
msgid "Confidence levels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:20
msgid "Categorize every finding:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "Criteria"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "Action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "**High**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Clearly unused, clearly duplicated, clearly wrong type, clearly "
"misleading comment. Removal/fix has no behavioral change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "Implement immediately"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "**Medium**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Likely an improvement but requires judgment — could affect behavior, "
"might break an edge case, or the \"right\" fix is debatable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "Document as recommendation, don't implement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "**Low**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "Stylistic, cosmetic, or would require significant restructuring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md
msgid "Mention in assessment only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:28
msgid "Rules for each concern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:30
msgid "Deduplication (DRY)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:31
msgid ""
"Only consolidate when the duplicated code is **genuinely the same "
"concern**, not just similar-looking code that happens to share structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:32
msgid ""
"Don't extract utilities for code that's duplicated only twice — wait for "
"three or more"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:33
msgid ""
"Don't create \"god util\" packages. Place shared code in the package that"
" owns the concept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:34
msgid ""
"If consolidation requires adding parameters or flags to handle variant "
"behavior, it's probably not worth it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:36
msgid "Type strengthening"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:37
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`any`/`interface{}` is legitimate for: JSON marshaling, database/sql "
"args, generic containers, protocol boundaries (MCP, GraphQL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:38
msgid ""
"Replace with concrete types when: the value is always used as one type, "
"or the set of types is small and known"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:39
msgid ""
"Don't create wrapper types just to avoid `any` — the cure shouldn't be "
"worse than the disease"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:40
msgid ""
"Check that replacement types are actually correct by tracing usage "
"upstream and downstream"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:42
msgid "Dead code removal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:43
msgid ""
"Verify with static analysis tools first (`deadcode`, `knip`, tree-shaking"
" analysis)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:44
msgid "Grep for all references before removing exported symbols"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:45
msgid ""
"Watch for: reflection, embed directives, interface implementations, build"
" tags, test helpers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:46
msgid "If uncertain, leave it and document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:48
msgid "Dependency structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:49
msgid "Go: no circular imports possible, focus on coupling and cohesion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:50
msgid "TypeScript/JS: use tools like `madge` to detect cycles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:51
msgid "Don't restructure working dependency graphs for cosmetic reasons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:52
msgid ""
"A \"god package\" that wires things together (CLI layer, main, app "
"bootstrap) is architecturally correct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:54
msgid "Defensive programming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:55
msgid ""
"Keep error handling for: user input, network I/O, file I/O, external "
"APIs, deserialization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:56
msgid ""
"Remove error handling that: swallows errors silently, returns fallback "
"values that mask bugs, catches panics without logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:57
msgid ""
"`_ = expr` is fine for: log writes, cache writes, cleanup operations, "
"non-critical side effects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:58
msgid ""
"`_ = expr` is not fine for: data writes the user expects to persist, "
"operations where failure means silent data loss"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:60
msgid "Legacy and fallback code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:61
msgid ""
"Backward compatibility for **user-facing config** is legitimate — don't "
"remove it without a migration path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:62
msgid ""
"Backward compatibility for **internal data formats** should be removed if"
" no deployments use the old format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:63
msgid ""
"Comments saying \"deprecated\" or \"legacy\" don't automatically mean the"
" code should be removed — check if it's still needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:64
msgid ""
"Feature flags and conditional paths that only have one active branch "
"should be simplified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:66
msgid "Comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:67
msgid ""
"Remove: narrating comments (\"increment counter\"), section dividers that"
" add nothing, AI boilerplate, work-in-progress references"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:68
msgid ""
"Keep: comments explaining **why** (not what), non-obvious algorithm "
"explanations, links to specs/tickets, license headers, godoc/JSDoc for "
"public APIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/code-scrub/SKILL.md:69
msgid ""
"Replace (don't just remove): misleading comments that describe behavior "
"the code doesn't have"
msgstr ""

